This product includes software developed with the following open-source
components (core profile):
- FastAPI (MIT), Starlette (BSD-3), Uvicorn (BSD-3)
- Pydantic (MIT), PyYAML (MIT), httpx (BSD-3)
- React (MIT), Vite (MIT), Recharts (MIT)

Optional full-profile detector adapters reference the following models and
libraries, downloaded separately by the user at their own election:
- cross-encoder/nli-MiniLM2-L6-H768 (Apache-2.0, sentence-transformers/UKPLab)
- unitary/toxic-bert (Apache-2.0, Unitary)
- Hugging Face transformers / optimum / onnxruntime (Apache-2.0 / MIT)

Evaluation design acknowledgements: injected-failure archetypes follow the
published methodology of public benchmarks — HaluEval and RAGTruth
(hallucination / unsupported assertion), JailbreakBench and garak (prompt
injection), Microsoft Presidio's recognizer taxonomy (PII formats). No
benchmark data is redistributed in this repository; all evaluation records
are synthetically generated (evals/generate.py, fixed seed).

The Verhoeff checksum implementation for Aadhaar-format validation follows the
public-domain algorithm description.
